"5cb1d607-78ca-599f-a42f-6cb360fcbf56" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the lines $-x - 4y =-4$ and $2x + 8y = 8$." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - 4y &=-4 \\\\ 2x + 8y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $-2x$ term that can cancel with the $2x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - 4y &=-4 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ 2x + 8y &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 8y &= -8 \\\\\n2x + 8y &= 8 \\\\\n0 &= (-8 + 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x - 4y &= -4 \\\\\n-4y &= -4 + x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-4 + x}{-4} \\\\\ny &= 1 - \\frac{1}{4}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(u,1 - \\frac{1}{4}u \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ec9eaf-8a8c-5485-9397-f4080cccdb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{2}{7}x - \\frac{6}{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542459} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc42961-0c2f-541f-bb32-0b326bb279c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542461} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab9055c-41fa-52d4-98cc-67b4d8dd46ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542484} {:answer/id #uuid "e29a0d02-5cca-5ff8-bf75-9db725841961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x - 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542502} {:answer/id #uuid "f097021f-ff70-5357-a6ad-89cefc4a73f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -\\frac{7}{2}x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dc42961-0c2f-541f-bb32-0b326bb279c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{7}{2}x + 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542461} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffc4aaed-af07-5113-8443-30d9a263ac17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ab21255-f04c-59e1-a7a8-fd7625364758" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the lines $-7x + 2y = 6$ and $-21x + 6y = 18$." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-7x + 2y &=6 \\\\ -21x + 6y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $21x$ term that can cancel with the $-21x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-7x + 2y &=6 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ -21x + 6y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n21x - 6y &= -18 \\\\\n-21x + 6y &= 18 \\\\\n0 &= (-18 + 18) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-7x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n2y &= 6 + 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{6 + 7x}{2} \\\\\ny &= 3 + \\frac{7}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,3 + \\frac{7}{2}x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0473f996-4e92-58c5-bd48-4ace42741c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}t + \\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0473f996-4e92-58c5-bd48-4ace42741c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}t + \\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542433} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e20b028-6414-53a2-a73b-b3e227d7d3fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7cd05dfa-1d47-5a9e-9f5f-9a75d2347390" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the lines $7x + 3y = 10$ and $21x + 9y = 30$. Express your answer in terms of $t$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are $(t$,\n{{field-1}}\n$)$, where $t$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 3y &=10 \\\\ 21x + 9y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $-21x$ term that can cancel with the $21x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 3y &=10 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ 21x + 9y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-21x - 9y &= -30 \\\\\n21x + 9y &= 30 \\\\\n0 &= (-30 + 30) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 3y &= 10 \\\\\n3y &= 10 - 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{10 - 7x}{3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{10}{3} - \\frac{7}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $t=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(t,\\frac{10}{3} - \\frac{7}{3}t \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa567d4-0454-5e1f-a013-55cfb13bce47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, \\frac{8}{5}u - \\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542449} {:answer/id #uuid "5496138f-4940-59c9-8cfa-4bf807aed2e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542468} {:answer/id #uuid "65af1755-d621-5206-b9fe-ee7a32a7810b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, \\frac{5}{8}u + \\frac{9}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542471} {:answer/id #uuid "b130be71-e990-5ee1-afcd-2de31bdb9cb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, \\frac{8}{5}u + \\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542488} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe07f49-e72f-5982-8433-a4f48f9fa695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{8}{5}u - \\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fa567d4-0454-5e1f-a013-55cfb13bce47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, \\frac{8}{5}u - \\frac{9}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542449} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2f7f9e0-a02a-57ec-baf6-911d39f91d52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9708e75-cf57-54fa-8a86-d6a41661f004" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the lines $-8x + 5y =-9$ and $16x - 10y = 18$." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x + 5y &=-9 \\\\ 16x - 10y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $-16x$ term that can cancel with the $16x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x + 5y &=-9 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ 16x - 10y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-16x + 10y &= -18 \\\\\n16x - 10y &= 18 \\\\\n0 &= (-18 + 18) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= -9 \\\\\n5y &= -9 + 8x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-9 + 8x}{5} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{9}{5} + \\frac{8}{5}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(u,-\\frac{9}{5} + \\frac{8}{5}u \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c60e70b-96f8-5431-90cd-a6ae562c2fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{6}x + \\frac{2}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542437} {:answer/id #uuid "0e35757a-2c57-5eb8-9b8e-33ffed7823b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542438} {:answer/id #uuid "1cef499e-0ec5-53e4-97d9-a3772813f69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x + 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542447} {:answer/id #uuid "4320905f-2597-5dbe-b58d-bb716941c26e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542463} {:answer/id #uuid "49b76269-cc41-593b-a5e2-31e2fd0a943a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e35757a-2c57-5eb8-9b8e-33ffed7823b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542438} :answer-field/id #uuid "10860ce5-13d5-5537-a83d-c826703c2441" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef3faa80-f6ae-5cf6-8c47-c5a225be4ccd" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the lines $6x - y = 4$ and $-24x + 4y =-16$." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - y &=4 \\\\ -24x + 4y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $24x$ term that can cancel with the $-24x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - y &=4 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ -24x + 4y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n24x - 4y &= 16 \\\\\n-24x + 4y &= -16 \\\\\n0 &= (16 - 16) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - y &= 4 \\\\\n-y &= 4 - 6x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4 - 6x}{-1} \\\\\ny &= -4 + 6x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-4 + 6x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cac595a2-a76f-5528-90a3-5b43bb6b6c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}t + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cac595a2-a76f-5528-90a3-5b43bb6b6c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}t + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542496} :answer-field/id #uuid "0052794e-29d0-5a14-847c-4f8656980f5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2d5e6d3-70ba-56f0-872c-ec4406eeabb5" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the lines $7x + 2y = 10$ and $21x + 6y = 30$. Express your answer in terms of $t$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are $(t$,\n{{field-1}}\n$)$, where $t$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 2y &=10 \\\\ 21x + 6y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $-21x$ term that can cancel with the $21x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 2y &=10 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ 21x + 6y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-21x - 6y &= -30 \\\\\n21x + 6y &= 30 \\\\\n0 &= (-30 + 30) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 2y &= 10 \\\\\n2y &= 10 - 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{10 - 7x}{2} \\\\\ny &= 5 - \\frac{7}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $t=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(t,5 - \\frac{7}{2}t \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e93e99b-7e76-59cd-a8bf-9d5a1e879a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e93e99b-7e76-59cd-a8bf-9d5a1e879a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542457} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f52dab6-f84a-51c1-bb5e-7609d7d43d80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd33d3a8-634b-5300-83fe-512c3febb665" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the lines $-3x - y =-4$ and $12x + 4y = 16$. Express your answer in terms of $t$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are $(t$,\n{{field-1}}\n$)$, where $t$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - y &=-4 \\\\ 12x + 4y &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $-12x$ term that can cancel with the $12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - y &=-4 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ 12x + 4y &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - 4y &= -16 \\\\\n12x + 4y &= 16 \\\\\n0 &= (-16 + 16) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x - y &= -4 \\\\\n-y &= -4 + 3x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-4 + 3x}{-1} \\\\\ny &= 4 - 3x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $t=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(t,4 - 3t \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d56e4e-14df-5e76-8811-2258751260f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{7}{5}u - \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542450} {:answer/id #uuid "2b767e80-1eaf-555b-9465-6842cf1181fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{7}{5}u + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542455} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdd62e8-0db4-5e13-9558-c017d95ac564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542478} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ea97ea-40ff-582c-b6e3-88f89d97fe8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, \\frac{7}{5}u + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542489} {:answer/id #uuid "c600e11f-1d2c-53ce-a422-159dac0d2e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{5}{7}u + \\frac{4}{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b767e80-1eaf-555b-9465-6842cf1181fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{7}{5}u + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542455} :answer-field/id #uuid "986fd8e2-7152-5f37-bea8-d024be1e25a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fec9f06c-a4db-563f-96a3-164f1364ae78" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the lines $7x + 5y = 4$ and $-14x - 10y =-8$." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 5y &=4 \\\\ -14x - 10y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $14x$ term that can cancel with the $-14x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 5y &=4 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ -14x - 10y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n14x + 10y &= 8 \\\\\n-14x - 10y &= -8 \\\\\n0 &= (8 - 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 5y &= 4 \\\\\n5y &= 4 - 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4 - 7x}{5} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{7}{5}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(u,\\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{7}{5}u \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is any number."}]}
